ok><name>WADA, HIROMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YONEMOTO, YOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIGAKI JUNJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATSUCHI MASAHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASAKI KEIZABURO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>URA SEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WADA HIROMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YONEMOTO YOSHIFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIGAKI, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATSUCHI, MASAHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KEIZABURO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>URA, SEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WADA, HIROMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YONEMOTO, YOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A communication system connected to the Internet through a communication network in which security is ensured, such as a cellular phone network and capable of lightening the load on a terminal for electronic commerce and banking service, wherein a ciphered communication request making unit (101) of a client device (100) sends a request of security of the communication path to a gateway server (200), a ciphered communication control unit (203) of the gateway server (200) sets up ciphered communication with a content server (300) in response to the request, the content server ciphers data to be transmitted to the client device and sends the cipphered data to the gateway server, the ciphered communication control unit of the gateway server deciphers the data and sends it to the client device. The client device requires no ciphering system, thereby lightening its load.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un système de communication qui est connecté à l'Internet par un réseau de communication où la sécurité est assurée, par exemple un réseau téléphonique cellulaire, et qui permet d'alléger la charge sur un terminal de commerce électronique et de services bancaires. L'unité de formulation de requête de communication chiffrée (101) d'un dispositif client (100) envoie une requête de sécurité de la voie de communication à un serveur passerelle (200). L'unité de commande de communication chiffrée (203) du serveur passerelle (200) établit la communication chiffrée avec un serveur de contenu (300) en réponse à la requête. Le serveur de contenu chiffre les données à transmettre au dispositif client, et envoie les données chiffrées au serveur passerelle. L'unité de commande de communication chiffrée du serveur passerelle déchiffre les données et les envoie au dispositif client. Le dispositif client n'a besoin d'aucun système de chiffrage-déchiffrage, ce qui permet d'alléger la charge sur ce dernier.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in a